IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ofek-domain`
IMPORT `ofek-salary-table`
IMPORT `ofek-placement`
IMPORT `ofek-worktime`
IMPORT `ofek-supplements`
IMPORT `ofek-fiscal-2025`
IMPORT `ofek-pay`

§ `Worked payslips`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Three teachers, computed end to end, with every figure traced back to the
-- article that produces it. These are the cases NOTES.md § 6 walks through in
-- prose; here they are as arithmetic that runs.
--
-- Every amount below was obtained by EVALUATING this encoding and then
-- written down, not computed by hand and hoped for. Where a figure looks
-- surprising — and the half-post case is designed to — the surprise is in the
-- instruments, not in the encoding.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `The dates the answers turn on`

`a month in the 2024 school year` MEANS YMD 2024 9 1
`a month in the first reduction period` MEANS YMD 2025 11 1
`a month in the second reduction period` MEANS YMD 2026 3 1
`a month after the school-role supplement begins` MEANS YMD 2026 10 1

§§ `Yael — a junior-high homeroom teacher, eleven years in`

-- BA, seniority 11, rank 4, a full post, homeroom teacher of a class other
-- than the first grade. She is the plainest case in the encoding, and every
-- later contrast is drawn against her.
--
--   combined salary        BA table, seniority 11, rank 4      9,171.76
--   Tosefet Ofek 2022      BA, rank 4, from 1.9.2023             835.54
--                                            the § 39 base    10,007.30
--   homeroom supplement    10% of that, being above the
--                          1,000 floor of 2022 § 10.1.1.2      1,000.73
--                                                             ---------
--                          before the reduction               11,008.03

#ASSERT `BA cell` 11 4 EQUALS 9_171.76
#ASSERT `the full-post percentage base for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 10_007.3
#ASSERT `the role supplements payable to` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 1_000.73
#ASSERT `the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 11_008.03

-- The floor of 2022 § 10.1.1.2 is only just idle here: 10% of her base is
-- 1,000.73 against a floor of 1,000. Seventy-three agora is the whole of the
-- margin, and a teacher one rank below her is inside the floor.
#ASSERT `the role supplements payable to` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` GREATER THAN `the floor under the homeroom supplement`

-- The reduction, in each of its two periods. § 9(a) takes 0.95% and § 9(b)
-- takes 1.2%, and the difference between the two months is 27.52 a month.
#ASSERT `the monthly pay of` `Yael` `a month in the first reduction period` 0 EQUALS 10_903.453715
#ASSERT `the monthly pay of` `Yael` `a month in the second reduction period` 0 EQUALS 10_875.93364
#ASSERT `the monthly pay of` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` 0 EQUALS 11_008.03

-- 2026 § 16, stacked on § 9. Had Yael advanced a seniority step worth 130 in
-- the September 2025 salary, she would have kept her new place in the table
-- and lost the whole cash value of it for four months, ON TOP of the 0.95%.
#ASSERT `the monthly pay of` `Yael` `a month in the first reduction period` 130 EQUALS 10_773.453715

-- And the withholding ends with 2025: the same step is hers to keep from
-- January 2026, when only the 1.2% is taken.
#ASSERT `the monthly pay of` `Yael` `a month in the second reduction period` 130 EQUALS 10_875.93364

§§ `Dvora — a primary-school teacher at the top of the table`

-- MA, seniority 30, rank 8, a full post, an existing teacher who converted.
-- She holds two role supplements, which is the § 39(c) maximum without the
-- district director, and three units of the 2022 § 22 school-role supplement.
--
--   combined salary        MA table, seniority 30, rank 8     15,537.52
--   Tosefet Ofek 2022      MA, rank 8, from 1.9.2023              37.37
--                                            the § 39 base    15,574.89
--   first-grade homeroom   11.5% of that                       1,791.11
--   subject coordinator    6% of that, primary school            934.49
--                                                             ---------
--                          before 1.9.2026                    18,300.50
--   school-role supplement 3 units at 200, flat                   600.00
--                                                             ---------
--                          from 1.9.2026                      18,900.50

#ASSERT `MA cell` 30 8 EQUALS 15_537.52
#ASSERT `the full-post percentage base for` `Dvora` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 15_574.89
#ASSERT `the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Dvora` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 18_300.49575
#ASSERT `the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Dvora` `a month after the school-role supplement begins` EQUALS 18_900.49575
#ASSERT `the monthly pay of` `Dvora` `a month after the school-role supplement begins` 0 EQUALS 18_673.689801

-- At rank 8 Tosefet Ofek 2022 has almost run out — 37.37 against the 1,585.54
-- a rank-1 BA teacher receives. That is the levelling § 5 was for, and it is
-- worth seeing as a ratio: the payment at the bottom of the table is more
-- than forty times the payment at the top of it.
#ASSERT `tosefet ofek 2022 from september 2023 in` `the BA table — rating code 101` 1 GREATER THAN (40 TIMES (`tosefet ofek 2022 from september 2023 in` `the MA table — rating code 102` 8))

-- The § 22 supplement is worth exactly 600 to her whatever else changes,
-- because it is neither a percentage nor pro-rated.
#ASSERT (`the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Dvora` `a month after the school-role supplement begins`) MINUS (`the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Dvora` `a month in the 2024 school year`) EQUALS 600

§§ `Noa — a doctorate on half a post`

-- MA table (§ 36(d)(1) places a doctorate there), seniority 6, rank 3, a new
-- teacher on half a post, no roles.
--
--   combined salary        MA table 6/3 = 8,440.10, halved      4,220.05
--   Tosefet Ofek 2022      MA rank 3 = 1,139.87, halved
--                          (2022 § 5.3 pro-rates it)              569.94
--   doctorate supplement   5% of her combined salary (§ 36(d)(2)) 211.00
--                                                             ---------
--                          before the reduction                5,000.99

#ASSERT `MA cell` 6 3 EQUALS 8_440.1
#ASSERT `the combined salary payable to` `Noa` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 4_220.05
#ASSERT `the tosefet ofek payable to` `Noa` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 569.935
#ASSERT `the doctorate supplement payable to` `Noa` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 211.0025
#ASSERT `the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Noa` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 5_000.9875

§§ `Half a post is not half the pay`

-- THE RESULT THIS ENCODING EXISTS TO MAKE VISIBLE. Take Yael and change one
-- field: half a post instead of a whole one. Nothing else about her moves.
`Yael on half a post` MEANS `a teacher` WITH
    `qualification`                IS `academic — holds a recognised first degree`
    `seniority in years`           IS 11
    `rank`                         IS 4
    `stage of education`           IS `a junior high school`
    `how they entered`             IS `a new teacher placed under section 36`
    `fraction of a full post`      IS 50%
    `roles`                        IS LIST `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade`
    `classes in the coordinated grade level` IS 0
    `units of the school-role supplement`    IS 0
    `teaches special education`    IS FALSE
    `special education percentage` IS 0

--   combined salary        halved                              4,585.88
--   Tosefet Ofek 2022      halved (2022 § 5.3)                   417.77
--   homeroom supplement    NOT halved (2008 § 39(b): the
--                          full-post figure, the post being
--                          at least a third)                   1,000.73
--                                                             ---------
--                                                              6,004.38
#ASSERT `the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Yael on half a post` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 6_004.38

-- 6,004.38 against 11,008.03 is 54.5% of the pay for 50% of the work. The
-- gap is the whole of the homeroom supplement, which § 39(b) directs be paid
-- at its full-post value to anybody employed for a third of a post or more.
#ASSERT (`the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Yael on half a post` `a month in the 2024 school year`) GREATER THAN ((50%) TIMES (`the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year`))

-- Stated exactly: the excess over half is the supplement, halved.
#ASSERT (`the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Yael on half a post` `a month in the 2024 school year`) MINUS ((50%) TIMES (`the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year`)) EQUALS ((50%) TIMES (`the role supplements payable to` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year`))

-- The same teacher just below the § 39(b) floor loses the supplement outright
-- and drops BELOW a proportionate share. A third of a post keeps it; a
-- thirtieth of a percent less loses it.
`Yael on just under a third of a post` MEANS `a teacher` WITH
    `qualification`                IS `academic — holds a recognised first degree`
    `seniority in years`           IS 11
    `rank`                         IS 4
    `stage of education`           IS `a junior high school`
    `how they entered`             IS `a new teacher placed under section 36`
    `fraction of a full post`      IS 0.33
    `roles`                        IS LIST `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade`
    `classes in the coordinated grade level` IS 0
    `units of the school-role supplement`    IS 0
    `teaches special education`    IS FALSE
    `special education percentage` IS 0

#ASSERT `the role supplements payable to` `Yael on just under a third of a post` `a month in the 2024 school year` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `the post carries the role supplements` 0.33
#ASSERT `the post carries the role supplements` (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

§§ `The value of an hour, and why the purpose matters`

-- 2008 § 31(a) prices a substitution hour off the combined salary alone, and
-- a school activity off the combined salary WITH the role supplements. For
-- Yael that is a difference of 6.42 an hour — a tenth of the hour's value —
-- turning only on which article the hour is worked under.
#ASSERT ROUND ((`the value of an hour for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` `a substitution hour`) TIMES 100) EQUALS 6420
#ASSERT ROUND ((`the value of an hour for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` `a school activity`) TIMES 100) EQUALS 7062
#ASSERT (`the value of an hour for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` `a school activity`) GREATER THAN (`the value of an hour for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` `a substitution hour`)

-- § 30(a) then pays a school activity at 125% of that, capped at 18 hours in
-- each half of the school year — so the most a school activity can add to
-- Yael's half-year is 1,588.92.
#ASSERT ROUND ((`the value of an hour for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` `a school activity`) TIMES `the rate for a school activity` TIMES `the school activity hours allowed in a half year` TIMES 100) EQUALS 158_892

-- And the 2026 agreement's additional hour is paid at a QUARTER of the hour's
-- value: 16.05 for an hour of teaching, against the 80.25 the same hour would
-- earn as an ordinary substitution.
#ASSERT ROUND ((`the pay for the section 25 additional hour` (`the value of an hour for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` `a substitution hour`) FALSE) TIMES 100) EQUALS 1605
#ASSERT ROUND ((`the value of an hour for` `Yael` `a month in the 2024 school year` `a substitution hour`) TIMES `the rate for a substitution hour` TIMES 100) EQUALS 8025

§§ `The reduction reaches a teacher's savings too`

-- 2026 § 12 reduces the study-fund base by the same rate, so the 1.2% is not
-- only taken from take-home pay.
#ASSERT ROUND ((`the study fund base after the reduction` (`the monthly pay before the reduction for` `Yael` `a month in the second reduction period`) `a month in the second reduction period`) TIMES 100) EQUALS 1_087_593

-- But § 18 keeps it out of the pension: an employer contribution is computed
-- as though nothing had been reduced.
#ASSERT `the reduction is ignored in computing` `an employer contribution to a pension fund`
#ASSERT `the reduction is ignored in computing` `the determining salary for a budgetary pension`

§§ `Promotion, on the same facts`

-- Yael is at rank 4. § 38(b)(4) asks three years' standing to reach rank 5,
-- and rank 5 is not rationed, so the ministry's criteria are the only other
-- condition.
`Yael applying for rank 5` MEANS `an application for promotion in rank` WITH
    `the current rank`                      IS 4
    `years of standing in the current rank` IS 3
    `the ministry criteria are met`         IS TRUE
    `the evaluations recommend promotion`   IS FALSE
    `the posts already at the rank sought`  IS 0
    `all teaching posts`                    IS 100_000
    `years already waited having qualified` IS 0

#ASSERT `the teacher may be promoted` `Yael applying for rank 5`
#ASSERT NOT (`the rank is rationed by quota` (`the rank sought by` `Yael applying for rank 5`))

-- Dvora is at rank 8 and applying for rank 9, which § 38(g) rations to 3% of
-- all posts. With 3,000 of 100,000 posts already at rank 9 there is no room,
-- however well she has been evaluated.
`Dvora applying for rank 9` MEANS `an application for promotion in rank` WITH
    `the current rank`                      IS 8
    `years of standing in the current rank` IS 4
    `the ministry criteria are met`         IS TRUE
    `the evaluations recommend promotion`   IS TRUE
    `the posts already at the rank sought`  IS 3_000
    `all teaching posts`                    IS 100_000
    `years already waited having qualified` IS 5

#ASSERT `the teacher meets the conditions for promotion` `Dvora applying for rank 9`
#ASSERT NOT `the quota admits the promotion` `Dvora applying for rank 9`
#ASSERT NOT `the teacher may be promoted` `Dvora applying for rank 9`

-- § 38(i)(3) says she may not be kept waiting more than five years having
-- qualified, and she has waited five. Both propositions hold at once, and the
-- agreement does not resolve them: NOTES.md § 5 records the tension.
#ASSERT `the teacher has waited as long as section 38(i) allows` `Dvora applying for rank 9`

-- One post fewer at rank 9 and the promotion goes through unchanged.
`Dvora applying for rank 9 with room` MEANS `an application for promotion in rank` WITH
    `the current rank`                      IS 8
    `years of standing in the current rank` IS 4
    `the ministry criteria are met`         IS TRUE
    `the evaluations recommend promotion`   IS TRUE
    `the posts already at the rank sought`  IS 2_999
    `all teaching posts`                    IS 100_000
    `years already waited having qualified` IS 5

#ASSERT `the teacher may be promoted` `Dvora applying for rank 9 with room`

§§ `The week, on the same facts`

-- Yael teaches in a junior high, so her full post is 23 frontal, 4 individual
-- and 9 presence hours (§ 17). Dvora's primary-school post is 26/5/5 (§ 15).
-- Both are 36 hours.
#ASSERT (`the ordinary full-post week in` (`Yael`'s `stage of education`))'s `frontal hours` EQUALS 23
#ASSERT (`the ordinary full-post week in` (`Dvora`'s `stage of education`))'s `frontal hours` EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `the hours in` (`the ordinary full-post week in` (`Yael`'s `stage of education`)) EQUALS `the hours in` (`the ordinary full-post week in` (`Dvora`'s `stage of education`))

-- Dvora converted from the pre-reform system, so at 56 she takes the larger
-- § 26(b) reduction. A new teacher of the same age takes the smaller one.
#ASSERT `the hours in` (`the week after the age reduction for` `Dvora` 56 (`the ordinary full-post week in` `a primary school`)) EQUALS 32
#ASSERT `the hours in` (`the week after the age reduction for` `Yael` 56 (`the ordinary full-post week in` `a junior high school`)) EQUALS 34
